Two patterns:

**Auto-paginate (return all)** — Tool handles pagination internally, returns the full list. Works for small datasets (<500 items). Simple for the agent, no extra round trips.

**Cursor-based** — Return a `next_cursor` when there are more results. Agent passes it back on the next call. Use when results can be large or unbounded.

For Jira issue search, cursor-based is safer — JQL can return thousands of results:

```typescript
// Tool returns:
{
  issues: Issue[],
  total: number,
  start_at: number,
  has_more: boolean  // agent uses this to decide whether to paginate
}

// Tool accepts:
{
  jql: string,
  max_results?: number,  // default 50
  start_at?: number      // cursor
}
```

Always include `total` and `has_more` — agents use these to decide whether more calls are needed.
